            <ArticleTitle>Leptin signaling in astrocytes regulates hypothalamic neuronal circuits and feeding.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>908-10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1038/nn.3725</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We found that leptin receptors were expressed in hypothalamic astrocytes and that their conditional deletion led to altered glial morphology and synaptic inputs onto hypothalamic neurons involved in feeding control. Leptin-regulated feeding was diminished, whereas feeding after fasting or ghrelin administration was elevated in mice with astrocyte-specific leptin receptor deficiency. These data reveal an active role of glial cells in hypothalamic synaptic remodeling and control of feeding by leptin.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
